    "subject": "N/A",
    "teaser": "",
    "entry": "Aberration presents as a plant bearing fruit that resemble watermelons. Vines grow from the watermelons in rapid fashion.",
    "notes": "Aberration is parasitic in nature. Its fruit, which resembles a watermelon, lures in its victim though scent. The victim then feels compelled to devour the entire fruit. After some time, the aberration will grow inside and rupture from the victim. The more victims that eat from the aberration, the more it can spread. Liquid inside the fruit are akin to digestive enzymes, similar to a Venus Flytrap. This indicates that, while the victim does eat the aberration, this is done so the aberration can eat the victim in return.",
